1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,180
In this exercise, you are asked to implement a function that visualizes a list of

2
00:00:06,180 --> 00:00:13,210
images in a grid and displays color-coded bounding boxes using Matplotlib.

3
00:00:14,750 --> 00:00:17,895
I started by reformatting

4
00:00:17,895 --> 00:00:23,640
our ground_truth input to a dictionary to make the data more accessible.

5
00:00:24,470 --> 00:00:28,650
I then created a Colormap, in this case,

6
00:00:28,650 --> 00:00:34,120
a dictionary that maps each class ID to a RGB triplet.

7
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:41,410
We can use the subplots function in Matplotlib to create a grid.

8
00:00:43,330 --> 00:00:49,530
We can loop through the different images to display them in the grid.

9
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:54,710
Using Matplotlib patches, we can display on each image,

10
00:00:54,710 --> 00:00:58,310
the different bounding boxes using the Colormap we created.

11
00:00:58,310 --> 00:01:04,860
Creating such visualization is extremely useful to better understand your data.

